-- title:
--   Values of the level-M/p pole chart at a cuspidal place
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\neq 0$ with $p\mid M$, $p^2\nmid M$, a subgroup $H\le(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image under `ZMod.unitsMap` for $(M/p)\mid M$ is $1$, and $M/p\neq 0$; assume $j$, as the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ`, lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be an `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` bundle, whose datum `Meta` is a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with function field $F_M=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, residue field $\kappa$ algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and $\rho:R_p\to A$ inducing the structure map $R_p\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $\mathrm{pb}$ be a unit of $\mathbb{Z}/(M/p)$ equal to $p$, and let $\delta$ act on places of $\mathrm{Fbar}=$ `qExpFunctionFieldC κ (ΓN p M H hpM)` as the semilinear automorphism attached to the diamond automorphism `diamondActionModL` at [`CuspForm.gammaLift (M / p) pb`](def/CuspForm_HeckeOperatorFormsGammaH.html#L36). Let $\theta$ be a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphism of $F_M$ which, by `hwgen`, describes on places the effect of precomposing points of `Meta.C` with $\mathfrak{X}.w$; let $\alpha:F_{M/p}\to F_M$ be a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra map which is the identity on underlying Laurent series, with $\alpha$ and $\theta\circ\alpha$ integral. Let $\mathrm{Psp}$ be a `JHPlaceSpecialization` datum, with specialization map $\mathrm{sp}$ from places of $F_{M/p}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to places of $\mathrm{Fbar}$ over $\kappa$, and $\mathrm{Rpd}$ a prolongation datum for $\mathrm{Psp}$ and $\theta$, consisting of regular prolongations $R_1,R_2$ of $A$ to $F_M$ with residues in $\mathrm{Fbar}$. Two compatibility hypotheses are assumed: `hres₂α`, that on elements $\alpha v$ integral for both $R_1$ and $R_2$ the $R_2$-residue is the $p$-power Frobenius `qExpFrobeniusModL` applied to the $R_1$-residue; and `hcomp`, that for $i\in\{0,1\}$ the place attached to a closed point of the fibre curve model $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Mfib}$ lying over the reduction of an $A$-section $u$ representing a point $y$ equals $\mathrm{Psp.reduceFst}\,\alpha$ of the place of $y$ when $i=0$, and $\mathrm{Psp.reduceSnd}$ for $\theta\circ\alpha$ and $\delta$ otherwise. Let $x'\in F_{M/p}$ have Laurent series `jqModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, let $S$ be the subring of $F_{M/p}$ generated by the constants from $A$ together with those elements whose Laurent series is the `coeffEmb` image of an element of the pole chart `chartAlgInf p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj`, and assume $\alpha$ maps $S$ into $R_1$'s integers. Then for every $b\in S$ and every place $w$ of $F_{M/p}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that $w.\mathrm{ord}(x'-a)\le 0$ for all $a\in A$, there exists $a\in A$ with $w$ taking the value $a$ at $b$, and with $\mathrm{Psp.sp}\,w$ taking the value $\bar a\in\kappa$ at the $R_1$-residue of $\alpha b$.
--
--   This is the statement that, at a place of the level-$M/p$ modular function field which is cuspidal in the sense that $j$ has no $A$-integral value there, the functions of the pole chart at infinity take values in $A$ and their specializations take the reduced values; the hypothesis `hcomp` is what ties the two reductions of the model at $p\parallel M$ to the place-specialization datum. It is used in [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_mul_eq_of_mem_integers_of_forall_sp_eq_cuspChartSetInf_prolongationDatum`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_mul_eq_of_mem_integers_of_forall_sp_eq_cuspChartSetInf_prolongationDatum), in the construction of the Deligne–Rapoport reduction of $X_H(M)$ at $p$ that underlies level lowering.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP_exists_hasValue_and_hasValue_sp_residue_of_mem_closure_chartAlgInf_of_cusp.lean

